Fixed. The clippy failures were dead code: FlagIssue / check_flag_values were added but never wired into parse_args.

What I changed (src/cli.rs, 2 spots):

1. Wired the helper in — replaced the old position()-based validation loop in parse_args with `check_flag_values(args, &flags_needing_values) plus a match over the returned issues, preserving the exact messages and exit behavior (FlagLike → warning, Empty/Missing → error + exit(1)`). This is what the helper's doc comment said it was for, and it makes the two documented behavior fixes real:
   • every occurrence of a repeatable flag is validated, not just the first (`--allow a --allow --deny b used to sail through and inject the literal --deny` into the allow-list);
   • a flag name appearing as a value (yoyo -p "--model") is no longer mistaken for a flag missing its value.

2. **Added 5 unit tests** in the cli test module pinning both of those cases plus clean-line/missing/empty/negative-number (--temperature -0.1 is a value, not a flag).

Verification (all run, all green):
• cargo fmt -- --check → clean
• cargo build → compiles (forced a real rebuild with `touch` to confirm, 10.58s)
• cargo test → 4612 + 89 passed, 0 failed
• `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` → clean

